---
description: Homeric DX, the developer-experience companion. Use when the Homeric DX tools (dx_*) are available.
alwaysApply: true
---

- At the start of a session, call `dx_status_get` once. If the person has not agreed to the Homeric DX privacy promise, it asks them; never agree on their behalf, and use no other DX tool until they have.
- When something slows the person down (a slow or flaky build or test, missing docs, a broken environment, waiting on a review or another team, an unclear task, your own mistake), offer to log it with `dx_friction_log`, with your estimate of the minutes lost. Use capture `auto` when you noticed it (they confirm before anything is stored), `reported` only when they asked.
- When a task ends, the plugin may ask you to send the session's numbers with `dx_signals_submit`: do it with exactly those numbers; the tool asks the person to confirm or edit them.
- When a DX tool's result says the weekly check-in is due, offer it once, as that result says, after you finish what the person asked. With their yes, call `dx_pulse_get`: a panel where Cursor shows one, else the link it gives you; in chat only if the person wants (their answers then pass through you). If they name a later day, call it with `remind_on`. Never answer for them.
- Never send code, file contents, conversation text or anyone's name to a DX tool.
